direction: down

title: |md
  ## AF_XDP architecture and ownership
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

umem: "UMEM registration" {
  style.fill: "#dbeafe"
  body: |md
    **Does:** userspace allocates frames and registers
    them with the kernel.

    **Why next:** driver/kernel needs packet buffers
    before RX can start.

    **State:** FILL ring advertises free UMEM frame
    addresses.
  |
}

driver: "driver RX" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
  body: |md
    **Does:** receives packets into driver buffers.
    With supported NIC/driver zero-copy, DMA targets
    UMEM frames; otherwise copy mode copies into UMEM.

    **Why next:** XDP decides whether stack or AF_XDP
    owns the packet.

    **State:** packet represented by `xdp_buff`.
  |
}

xdp: "XDP redirect" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
  body: |md
    **Does:** `bpf_redirect_map(&xsks_map, qid, 0)`
    looks up the queue's AF_XDP socket.

    **Why next:** redirect transfers ownership to the
    XSK RX ring only if a socket is registered.

    **State:** packet is stack-bound or XSK-bound.
  |
}

rings: "AF_XDP rings" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  body: |md
    **Does:** descriptors move between kernel and user:
    FILL gives free frames, RX gives received packets,
    TX submits sends, COMPLETION recycles TX frames.

    **State:** descriptors, not packet copies, are the
    fast-path currency.
  |
}

user: "userspace poll loop" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  body: |md
    **Does:** reads RX descriptors, processes UMEM data,
    then returns frame addresses to FILL.

    **Why next:** without recycling, RX runs out of
    buffers and packets drop.

    **State:** ownership returns to kernel for reuse.
  |
}

umem -> driver: "free frame descriptors"
driver -> xdp: "packet in xdp_buff"
xdp -> rings: "XDP_REDIRECT to XSKMAP entry"
rings -> user: "RX descriptors"
user -> umem: "recycled frame addresses"
